'''Line C''' of the [[CristoCarril]] (CC) system is a commuter rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that runs on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor between the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Varakí Central (CristoCarril)|Varakí Central]] in [[Varakí]]. The line covers 65.7 km and serves 26 stations across two comarcas — [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]]. It is the third CristoCarril line, complementing [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] on the [[Coastal Line]] corridor and [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] on the [[Portnou Line]] corridor.

Line C follows an inland route southward from the Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal, through the eastern ciutats of Sant Cristòfor — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]], and [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]] — before entering the Cumará comarca and serving the municipalities of [[La Cruïlla]] and [[Varakí]]. The line shares the Varakí Line tracks with [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 4 (RdP L4), which provides local services between Varakí and the Portnou metropolitan area.

== Route ==

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

Line C begins at the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], the city's primary rail hub, shared with [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]]. From the terminal, the line heads south through three stations in Original — [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]], [[Sant Pere (CristoCarril)|Sant Pere]], and [[La Font (CristoCarril)|La Font]] — serving the dense residential neighbourhoods south of the historic core. These four stations are shared with Line B, which diverges at La Font to follow the Portnou Line corridor through [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] and [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]], while Line C continues on the Varakí Line corridor through the eastern ciutats.

The line then enters [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], where it serves seven stations: [[Centre de Metro (CristoCarril)|Centre de Metro]], [[Centre Comercial Hiro (CristoCarril)|Centre Comercial Hiro]], [[Turó Vermell (CristoCarril)|Turó Vermell]], [[Carretera de Martí (CristoCarril)|Carretera de Martí]], [[Unió Cr (CristoCarril)|Unió Cr]], [[Plaça de la Catedral (CristoCarril)|Plaça de la Catedral]], and [[Divisió Cr (CristoCarril)|Divisió Cr]]. Sant Jordi is a densely populated residential ciutat on the eastern side of Sant Cristòfor, and these stations provide the primary commuter rail connection for its neighbourhoods.

Continuing south, the line passes through seven stations in [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]] — [[Persepolis Cr (CristoCarril)|Persepolis Cr]], [[Cresta del poble (CristoCarril)|Cresta del poble]], [[Campana Aerodrom (CristoCarril)|Campana Aerodrom]], [[Oest Cr (CristoCarril)|Oest Cr]], [[Beaumon (CristoCarril)|Beaumon]], [[Paria (CristoCarril)|Paria]], and [[Torrepolis (CristoCarril)|Torrepolis]]. The line then enters [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]], serving three stations: [[Autopista 58 (CristoCarril)|Autopista 58]], [[Carretera de Torres (CristoCarril)|Carretera de Torres]], and [[Plaça Mario (CristoCarril)|Plaça Mario]]. The 22 stations within Sant Cristòfor cover the eastern and southern districts of the city, serving dense residential and commercial areas.

=== Cumará ===

After leaving Sant Cristòfor, Line C enters the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]] and serves the municipality of [[La Cruïlla]], a suburban municipality with a population of over 351,000. The line stops at three stations in La Cruïlla: [[Torre Fàcil (CristoCarril)|Torre Fàcil]], [[Autopista 68/La Cruïlla (CristoCarril)|Autopista 68/La Cruïlla]], and [[Carretera Udi (CristoCarril)|Carretera Udi]]. The La Cruïlla stations form a commuter pair with the Ciutat de l'Estació stations in Sant Cristòfor, generating significant bidirectional peak-period traffic.

The line then enters the municipality of [[Varakí]], the largest city in Cumará with a population of over 852,000 and the capital of the comarca. The line serves two stations in Varakí: [[Varakí TDV (CristoCarril)|Varakí TDV]], a major interchange station connecting to the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR]] and [[Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR line|Sant Cristòfor–Areza HSR]] lines; and [[Varakí Central (CristoCarril)|Varakí Central]], the city's principal rail hub, shared with [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 4. Varakí Central is the southern terminus of Line C.

