== Service pattern ==

Line C operates three service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Varakí]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Short''' || All stops 1–18 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Torrepolis || ~42 min
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 5, 10, 18, 25, 26 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Varakí Central, skipping intermediate stations || ~60 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–26 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Varakí Central || ~77 min
|}

The '''short''' service operates entirely within [[Sant Cristòfor]], running from the Central Terminal through the eastern ciutats — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]], and [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]] — to Torrepolis on the southern edge of Sant Martí. This is the most frequent service, providing high-capacity commuter rail for the dense residential districts of eastern Sant Cristòfor.

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and Varakí, stopping at the Central Terminal, Portal de Sant Cristòfor, Centre de Metro, Plaça de la Catedral, Torrepolis, Varakí TDV, and Varakí Central. The express skips most suburban stations within Sant Cristòfor and all intermediate stations in La Cruïlla, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 60 minutes. The express is primarily used by long-distance commuters between the two cities and passengers connecting to intercity services at Varakí TDV.

The '''local''' service stops at all 26 stations along the full 65.7 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 77 minutes. The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Sant Martí, Ciutat de l'Estació, and La Cruïlla. Between Varakí TDV and Varakí Central, the line shares tracks with [[Rodalies de Portnou]] Line 4, which provides local services continuing south to the Portnou metropolitan area.

== Schedule ==

Line C operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Short''' || every 10 min || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 20 min (daytime), every 30 min (evening)
|-
| '''Express''' || every 20 min || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 30 min (daytime), every 60 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|}

The short service is the most frequent, reflecting the high commuter demand within eastern Sant Cristòfor. The express provides a regular connection between Sant Cristòfor and Varakí, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in outer Sant Cristòfor and La Cruïlla. Combined, the three services provide up to 12 trains per hour at the Central Terminal during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line C uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line operates a flat fare of B$2.50 for all journeys, regardless of distance travelled.

Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

